{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming","id":1500606,"title":"Abyssals are coming!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-18T07:41:58-08:00","id":1500606,"title":"Abyssals are coming!","content":"So since we last had a forum we've had Kickstarters for both Exigents and Sidereals.<br /> <br /> With the Deathknights up next what are people hoping for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T09:10:32-08:00","id":1500611,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping for several things<br /> <br /> 1. Extensive details on the Underworld, deathlords and the different kinds of undead in creation<br /> 2. Varied types of abyssals beyond just deathknights for the deathlords. Lets have some variety, even while we keep that as the dominate type.<br /> 3. Necromancy as a fully functioning system analogous to sorcery. This will require some serious flexibility and creative uses of death magic, but I'm there for it<br /> 4. Some interesting exploration of the romantic, poetic and aesthetic themes around the abyssals.<br /> <br /> I'm currently writing a game starring abyssal PCs and although I'm able to do a lot of prep, the massive hole where any abyssal lore and necromancy rules means there is a lot I can't fill in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T12:01:51-08:00","id":1500630,"title":"","content":"oh, I'm definitely looking forward to seeing 3rd Edition's take on the Underworld and the Abyssal's relationship with it. Hopefully also a closer look at the sorts of societies that form around shadowlands like Perch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26730-tomdick-harry","name":"TomDick&Harry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T18:12:56-08:00","id":1500686,"title":"","content":"I don't even know. I liked the old Abyssals as dark mirrors of the Solars. New Abyssals will have fully remade and re-imagine powersets more in line with the Sidereal Exalted (in that Charms and Abilities will be themed after a specific being, in this case various Deathlords) so I don't even know whether I'll like it or not and what I want or not. They're just too different from the old Abyssals, mechanically, and in terms of theme and mood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T03:13:44-08:00","id":1500712,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping to see powers and abilitites that really break away from them just being dark mirrors of the Solars. I think thats always going to be an unmistakable part of their theme, but I want to see Charms that aren't Heavenly Guardian Defense and Harmonious Presence Method painted Goth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T12:01:49-08:00","id":1500753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1500686#post1500686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even know. I liked the old Abyssals as dark mirrors of the Solars. New Abyssals will have fully remade and re-imagine powersets more in line with the Sidereal Exalted (in that Charms and Abilities will be themed after a specific being, in this case various Deathlords) so I don't even know whether I'll like it or not and what I want or not. They're just too different from the old Abyssals, mechanically, and in terms of theme and mood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Death's Lawgivers is one of their epithets, and there'll be Charms that reflect that side of their nature per Vance, raising up empires of the dead and imposing order on the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T13:33:52-08:00","id":1500768,"title":"","content":"Lessee, most of mine have been mentioned already. Necromancy, awesome Underworld deets, etc.<br /> <br /> Lizard Style and Scorpion Style martial-arts, though that's a general &quot;book that isn't out&quot; hope.<br /> <br /> The return of the Soul Mirror (Evocations would fit its power set spectacularly)<br /> <br /> A more in depth look at the culture around death and funerary rights across Creation. (I'm a sucker for neat setting flavor like that)<br /> <br /> A cool &quot;Here's plot ideas&quot; section like Heaven got in Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Systems to better support climbing around like a spider monkey on gargantuan foes like Juggernaut. Mahicara has some solid stuff, but it doesn't fully scratch that &quot;Shadow of the Colossus: Exalted Edition&quot; itch<br /> <br /> And, last but most certainly not least...<br /> GIVE US ALBICANT SEPULCHER OF EXTINCTION STYLE YOU F*CKING COWARDS! (\u251b\u25c9\u0414\u25c9)\u251b\u5f61\u253b\u2501\u253b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T03:12:42-08:00","id":1500913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1500686#post1500686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New Abyssals will have fully remade and re-imagine powersets more in line with the Sidereal Exalted (in that Charms and Abilities will be themed after a specific being, in this case various Deathlords) so I don't even know whether I'll like it or not and what I want or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there something I don't know about displayed in Essence or mentioned on Discord?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T05:35:00-08:00","id":1500921,"title":"","content":"It feels like a variation of the &quot;they're turning Infernals into Abyssals and Abyssals into Infernals&quot; rhetoric that's been with us since 2014, which is partially the fault of how Morke wrote that part of the preview like an essay discussing Abyssal themes rather than addressing players who wanted their favourite splat to be good this time around.<br /> <br /> Abyssals have <b>always</b> done things that didn't line up 1:1 with themes of 'Death' and 'Oblivion' because they're so limiting. MoEP: Abyssals, for example gave greater prominence to the Neverborn and their desire to have the Abyssals be something worse than the Deathlords that 2e wasn't really able to deliver on, an idea that was recycled to better effect in Infernals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T16:07:36-08:00","id":1500967,"title":"","content":"I think it depends a lot on what one means out of Abyssals being dark mirrors of Solars. Like, what was Second Edition Resistance like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T23:29:48-08:00","id":1501011,"title":"","content":"Look, &quot;Dark Mirror Solars&quot; is a viable vector for Abyssals, but it should represent the most basic elements of the splat at best. The Black Sun of Oblivion is one heck of a solid foundation. But it works best as only a foundation. I can see Essence 1 charms looking a lot like that. Just a few twists and tweaks, as this is the point where it is closest to being a Solar, only as nods to their new themes. The low level bread and butter charms that are already boring are arguably the best fit for &quot;Mirror&quot; charms<br /> <br /> Beyond Essence 1, (so 2-3+), they should be informed more by their own themes, as the Exaltation starts to grow beyond it's former existence. The seed of Deathly essence has begun to sprout. Filtering the Essence through the Deathlords means that the charms should start looking that way here. The 'Deathlords substituting for the Unconquered Sun' should be felt in their charm design at this point.<br /> <br /> At the capstones (Essence 5+) however, we should see this unholy combination grow beyond expectations. Not only not mirrors of Solars but even breaking away from the Deathlords here. This is where I would hope to see the Deathknights surpass their overlords. This should also be where their charms are the furthest from their Solar counterparts. Get weird, give us ghost stories and nightmare fuel. This is where I'd hope to see the nihilism really show itself for the first time, but it shouldn't be the only option. <br /> <br /> Heck questions like &quot;how does this Ability deal with Death, interact with the Dead or even Die itself?&quot; should be not only asked but even answered at various points of the charm tree and looking at how Deathlords themselves would answer those questions could be helpful at filling out the charm trees. <br /> <br /> Ok, so that is way too much about the Abyssal charmset, particularlysince I hope to get a better view of how the Underworld is ruled/'lived in' from this book, in addition to a nice big chonky set of descriptions about how Necromancy differs from Sorcery, even if i expect the rules to basically be a copy/paste kind of deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T02:04:11-08:00","id":1501017,"title":"","content":"See, I look back at those previewed Socialise Charms, and to me it looked like the stuff that would map in the most straightforward fashion to what the Solars got was not the least powerful stuff, and then the parts that developed off in directions unique to the Abyssals... if you know who the Lover Clad in the Raiment of Tears was you can see that as a template in the vampiric/ghostly seduction stuff, but if you don't know the Deathlord then does it seem any less natural as an expression of that Ability for Gothic romance heroes of death?<br /> <br /> What does a person want out of being dark mirrors of the Solars? To have Charms that function in very similar manner but creepier aesthetics, or to look at the thematic concept of what Solars are, create a dark counterpart to that, and then give them Charms that organically express that image?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-23T18:03:29-08:00","id":1501193,"title":"","content":"Certainly would be nice for the Deathlords to not be all Solar Ghosts so crossing my fingers this is alluded to in the new edition. It feels like 3rd Edition has done a really good job of leveling the playing field for all the splats available so it would be nice to see some actual middle ground stories instead of choosing between Edge-lord Renegade Solar Wannabe's and Murder-hobo Loyalists. Also i really liked Adversaries of the Righteous Abyssal NPC's and thought they were going in a pretty good direction with the possibilities and it would be refreshing to see it continue. <br /> <br /> While i enjoy the idea of some charms being dark mirrors to the Solars i do feel a charm-set that expresses Abyssals as unique entities of the setting would be a breath of fresh air. Even a newish sort of take on the world they live in that isnt completely married to the idea of killing creation (even if that is some sort of end goal for the Neverborn). <br /> <br /> and lastly just hoping for a really dope looking black book. this is my favorite splat so gotta say i am pretty pumped about the possibilities <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27008-masque","name":"Masque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27008_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T08:14:46-08:00","id":1501234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Masque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1501193#post1501193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly would be nice for the Deathlords to not be all Solar Ghosts so crossing my fingers this is alluded to in the new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div> In Charting Fate's Course there's a blurb that seems to allude to the Bishop possibly originally being a Sidereal. &quot;Among the Exalted, only Sidereals, Getimians, Solars, Abyssals, and Infernals can learn Sidereal Martial Arts. Some rare or unique beings may also be able to learn them or even create them at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion \u2014 for example, the Deathlord known as the Bishop of the Chalcedony Thurible can use Sidereal Martial Arts and has created the Albicant Sepulcher of Extinction style, a bleak expression of the Neverborn\u2019s feverish desire for total destruction.&quot; And two paragraphs latter we get &quot;Only Sidereals are capable of learning Sidereal Martial Arts without a mentor and creating new styles. Other characters must seek out a Sidereal\u2019s tutelage.&quot; While the Bishop could indeed be just one of those &quot;Rare and unique beings&quot;, but the sidebar taken as a whole certainly opens the idea that what made the Bishop able to craft the style is he WAS a Sidereal originally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-24T13:14:13-08:00","id":1501258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1500921#post1500921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels like a variation of the &quot;they're turning Infernals into Abyssals and Abyssals into Infernals&quot; rhetoric that's been with us since 2014, which is partially the fault of how Morke wrote that part of the preview like an essay discussing Abyssal themes rather than addressing players who wanted their favourite splat to be good this time around.<br /> <br /> Abyssals have <b>always</b> done things that didn't line up 1:1 with themes of 'Death' and 'Oblivion' because they're so limiting. MoEP: Abyssals, for example gave greater prominence to the Neverborn and their desire to have the Abyssals be something worse than the Deathlords that 2e wasn't really able to deliver on, an idea that was recycled to better effect in Infernals.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were some interesting ideas apart of the underlying &quot;Dark Solar Mirror&quot; ones, it's just that they were only shallowly touched and were not given enough emphasis. The Abomination charms were something distinct, a nice idea hinting at a transhumanism path that was completely Abyssal one, without any hint of Solar influences. Avatar (whispers-tied) ones were a lot more of hit-and-miss (and i was never very fond of how the Abyssals were so obsessively tied to Oblivion), but they also were a hint for a separate path. And i agree that similar themes (especially for Abomination path) eventually made it to Infernals, in a more fleshed out way. What 2e Abyssals <i>seriously</i> lacked however were more pronounced ties to underworld and ghosts. That's one of the reasons why they ended up as Solars painted black, and not as Champions of Death. Hope this time it will be addressed far better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T10:59:10-08:00","id":1501325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1501258#post1501258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What 2e Abyssals <i>seriously</i> lacked however were more pronounced ties to underworld and ghosts. That's one of the reasons why they ended up as Solars painted black, and not as Champions of Death. Hope this time it will be addressed far better.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's ironic because at the time the insistence was that Abyssals were &quot;Champions of Death, not of the Dead&quot; and that a character invested in Necromancy/the Underworld who wasn't onboard the apocalypse train was a &quot;Spooky Solar&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T11:53:35-08:00","id":1501334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1501325#post1501325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's ironic because at the time the insistence was that Abyssals were &quot;Champions of Death, not of the Dead&quot; and that a character invested in Necromancy/the Underworld who wasn't onboard the apocalypse train was a &quot;Spooky Solar&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue being that what Abyssals were geared to be in 2e - the ultimate killers, created from inverted Solar Exaltations, and intended to kill the world - is, well, a weak foundation to build on for a whole splat's Charmset; you need more than that to articulate the Abyssal Charmset as something distinctive in its own right. Morke was onto something with having the Deathlords as major sources of Abyssal Charm themes, if nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T13:41:14-08:00","id":1501341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1501325#post1501325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's ironic because at the time the insistence was that Abyssals were &quot;Champions of Death, not of the Dead&quot; and that a character invested in Necromancy/the Underworld who wasn't onboard the apocalypse train was a &quot;Spooky Solar&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That devs insisted on this approach was not the problem by itself. Champions of Death done well could have worked too. Problem is, it was being tone by just giving them charms to kill things better. In a pretty much direct way. Abyssals thus ended up being less Champions of Death, and more just Murderhobos - exalts that are very good at <i>killing</i>, which is not exactly the same. And the fact that Solars were already very good at doing the exact same thing, when they put their minds to it, definitely didn't make things any better. And as for being invested in Necromancy/Underworld... again, there was no significant difference between that and Solars doing the same. Except that often Solars were even <i>better</i> at it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-25T23:02:59-08:00","id":1501375,"title":"","content":"The Monstrances aren't a thing anymore I hope. Or at least the whole, &quot;If your solar gets shoved in one you're only option to not become an abyssal is to unalive yourself, so your exaltation doesn't permanently become an abyssal one. And pray your next life ends better.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T02:18:17-08:00","id":1501387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1501375#post1501375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Monstrances aren't a thing anymore I hope. Or at least the whole, &quot;If your solar gets shoved in one you're only option to not become an abyssal is to unalive yourself, so your exaltation doesn't permanently become an abyssal one. And pray your next life ends better.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's ways to implement the Monstrance of Celestial Portion in a way that focuses the experience on the Exalt trapped inside it but question the use of that space in a book that's supposed to be about playing Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T06:38:56-08:00","id":1501399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1501375#post1501375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Monstrances aren't a thing anymore I hope. Or at least the whole, &quot;If your solar gets shoved in one you're only option to not become an abyssal is to unalive yourself, so your exaltation doesn't permanently become an abyssal one. And pray your next life ends better.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like monstrances because as soon as they are introduced, there is an epic quest target. Solars can go after monstrances to try and free the exaltations. Rogue Abyssals can try and steal their own to stop the deathlords controlling them. Loyalists can have their own monstrances get stolen and they have to track the thieves down before they do whatever it is they stole it for. They are excellent plot hooks.<br /> As a GM I'd never put a PC in one with their own option being to kill themselves. Thats not a fun game. Its a fun threat for baddies to make though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-26T09:12:37-08:00","id":1501410,"title":"","content":"One of the big things I noticed right off the bat when I first got the 3e core book is that there wasn't a stat block for Mask of Winters like there was in 1e and 2e. Pretty understandable since Deathlords and Deathknights are both undergoing an overhaul so they aren't just &quot;Spooky Solars&quot; that get a serotonin boost from killing stuff. Though, I think having the Deathlords statted out (either one, some, or all) would give players and storytellers alike an idea of their power scale. Though I'll probably end up converting MoW into a QC on my own if I I ever end up needing him for a scene or three. Considering he's a hated rival of one of my players' characters, it's bound to happen sooner or later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13277-angelwick","name":"AngelWick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T01:46:19-08:00","id":1501522,"title":"","content":"I want the Eye and Seven Despairs to be based exclusively on 1st edition material and new ideas, ignoring the 2nd edition additions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-28T11:43:57-08:00","id":1501553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1501522#post1501522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want the Eye and Seven Despairs to be based exclusively on 1st edition material and new ideas, ignoring the 2nd edition additions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance's said they're dropping Eye's mind games with his Abyssals (which were a 1e and 2e sin), and he'll be playing the gothic mad scientist to the hilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T07:30:08-08:00","id":1501608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1501553#post1501553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vance's said they're dropping Eye's mind games with his Abyssals (which were a 1e and 2e sin), and he'll be playing the gothic mad scientist to the hilt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good to me. I actually liked the concept of Eye and Seven Despairs being dead and his Abyssals running the show. It made for a very different, but interesting player experience, when their &quot;bosses&quot; are just a year or two older than the PCs are and the PCs are able to very quickly surpass them in their areas of expertise. Plus there's a lot of potential in the idea of having powerful, ancient ghosts, and other creatures subservient to the Deathlord, but still stronger than, or at least dangerous to, a young Abyssal wondering where the boss is, and the Abyssal has to try and keep everything going without it all collapsing like a house of cards (a more serious and deadly version of Weekend at Bernies).<br /> <br /> But then the actual implementation was awkward because Eye wasn't actually dead, he was just fucking around so there was basically one direction that that sort of plot was going to go. In the end, getting rid of all that, starting over and re-imagining Eye and Seven Despairs and his role in the setting seems like a good idea to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T03:17:42-08:00","id":1501685,"title":"","content":"I'd personally want the Monstrances to stick around in their capacity as the vessel in which Abyssal Essences are kept between incarnations because I think it's an evocative image that lends itself well to the whole Gothic Underworld aesthetic and because I like the idea that the Deathlords need an intermediary instrument to manage the whole Choosing side of it while they're less than the stature of an Incarna.<br /> <br /> Sometimes I wonder if people assume that they're called that as a kind of modification of the word &quot;monster&quot;, rather than monstrances being an actual thing used in Christian ceremonies, an alter vessel used for the display of the Eucharistic host. It comes from the Latin word meaning &quot;to show&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T08:49:08-08:00","id":1501711,"title":"","content":"I think they can serve a worthwhile purpose, it's just a question of if they're ingrained in people's minds as torture devices and killswitches for unruly Deathknights that retaining and rehabilitating them might be more trouble than it's actually worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T11:54:02-08:00","id":1501734,"title":"","content":"Vance's said monstrances are sticking around (in no small part for their aesthetics). No killswitches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T04:22:01-08:00","id":1501801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1501553#post1501553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vance's said they're dropping Eye's mind games with his Abyssals (which were a 1e and 2e sin), and he'll be playing the gothic mad scientist to the hilt.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mind games were fine.<br /> <br /> In 1st he was described as perhaps the most dangerous Deathlord of them all.<br /> <br /> But in 2nd edition he is an absent-minded buffoon, his name has a super lame origin*, the mind games have a convoluted origin, and there is just so much latent transphobia surrounding the character.<br /> <br /> *The ancient-ass Solars tortured the young Solar in seven unspeakably horrific ways and then they presented him with the eye of his father and he killed himself. What were the seven despairs that were, presumably, less horrific than that?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":864,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","user":"Jutlander","date":". 01-31-2023, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T05:51:37-08:00","id":1501866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1501801#post1501801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mind games were fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>They weren't problematic like the other elements but they were a potential obstacle to using him because it was common knowledge among the fanbase that reports of his demise were greatly exaggerated.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T19:47:09-08:00","id":1501996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1501734#post1501734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vance's said monstrances are sticking around (in no small part for their aesthetics). No killswitches.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine some Deathlords would suggest or imply that a Monstrance <i>could</i> serve as a killswitch, but it's important that the game make a clear out-of-character distinction that that isn't the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T21:02:01-08:00","id":1502081,"title":"","content":"I feel like starting off a relationship by saying 'you will literally die if you don't do what I say because I have a magic murder monstrance' wouldn't be a great way to build the kind of working relationship you want with an exalted servant. Its a very poor motivator for getting them to put in anything beyond the absolute bare minimum they need to skate by on your assignments while looking around for ways to ditch your ass as soon as they figure out how to disarm the metaphorical bomb collar around their neck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T13:38:53-08:00","id":1502134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming#post1500606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the Deathknights up next what are people hoping for?</div> </div> </div> </div>That the existence of Liminals (which I like) won't trick the writers into taking body horror out of the Abyssal Charmset. They had &quot;turn all of your blood into armour&quot; as a Charm in 1e; more of that shit.<br /> <br /> That the combat Charms are sufficiently gory and atrocious.<br /> <br /> And, pipe dream of pipe dreams, that we get some new deathlords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T14:42:27-08:00","id":1502147,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I would rather they focus on reworking the 9 existing deathlords and making them interesting to work for honestly. I mean, I can see why you would want something completely new instead of just reworking old content. But personally I worry that adding more would hurt the final product in terms of how much word count each deathlord gets to flesh them out and in terms of finding ways to keep them unique from each other since it increases the number of characters they need to find a compelling concept for that sets working for them apart from working for the others. Personally I'm fine with just considering any sufficiently altered deathlord to be a new character in terms of getting new things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T15:53:15-08:00","id":1502158,"title":"","content":"I'd settle for just one-paragraph blurbs like the little location writeups in Fangs at the Gate and the Realm, or even something like the sidebar on potential additional Seven Storms members in WFHW.<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, in the ideal world we'd cut some old cruft, but that is not and was never happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T00:25:48-08:00","id":1502182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1502158#post1502158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd settle for just one-paragraph blurbs like the little location writeups in Fangs at the Gate and the Realm, or even something like the sidebar on potential additional Seven Storms members in WFHW.<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, in the ideal world we'd cut some old cruft, but that is not and was never happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the issue with them in 1e is they were too much like variatns on Mask of Winters and in 2e, they didn't do a lot to change that save adding a lot of edge, and kind of setting deep lore to them that didn't hlep. It's notable to me that for example, the stuff on Walker in Darkness we have seen mentioen from devs derives a lot more from a kind of one-off bit of him making Faustian deals in the Underworld book, which was not how he was characterized before to my memory, and sure as shit sin't the bumbling idiot he is in 1e and 2e's usual depictions of him.<br /> <br /> The Deathlords as a whole honestly have some good core aesthetic, conceptual, and thematic elemnts. The cruft is more what is built around those and how to use them. ANd just kind of tossing them and making new ones isn't really as useful when they all have their kind of tendrils somewher,e unlike some Lunar elders who wre kind of stapleed-on. (As much as folks like Tamuz for example, he's kind of irrrelevant as he wasn't important for Chiaroscuro being that unitl it was retconned to him, and the things in 1e and 2e he's trying to be a solution or foil to are just not there anymore.)<br /> <br /> Now, new ones aren't precluded, but my guess is we'll see the traditional canon nine given treatments akin to shahan-ya in Lunars or a DB hosue or society in those books. Anything then beyond that probably will be more akin to something more like a story hook or textbox like the aformentioend bit with the Seven Thunders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T06:43:27-08:00","id":1502302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1502081#post1502081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like starting off a relationship by saying 'you will literally die if you don't do what I say because I have a magic murder monstrance' wouldn't be a great way to build the kind of working relationship you want with an exalted servant. Its a very poor motivator for getting them to put in anything beyond the absolute bare minimum they need to skate by on your assignments while looking around for ways to ditch your ass as soon as they figure out how to disarm the metaphorical bomb collar around their neck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again I don't think it's something most Deathlords would do, but I think it's something that a Deathlord <i>could</i> do. <br /> <br /> I'd expect that there a host of different ways that Deathlords would interact with their vassals, but that could include a Skeletor-like Deathlord who threatens to (and maybe sometimes does) murder minions for failure. That's a fairly classic evil overlord trope and can create fairly good drama for a campaign if a player is subservient to that sort of a ruler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T04:00:54-08:00","id":1502820,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Dark Reaper Style could be salvaged as a Martial Art separate from giving Abyssals back a Brawl cascade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T21:18:37-08:00","id":1503729,"title":"","content":"Okay, one more thing I want from 3E Abyssals. That's for Angela Sasser's awesome design for the Lover to be canonized. Because seriously, how fucking cool is THAT?!<br /> <img width=\"1200\" height=\"900\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.redd.it/zn13tp8rd8z51.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.redd.it/zn13tp8rd8z51.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.redd.it/zn13tp8rd8z51.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T15:49:29-08:00","id":1504081,"title":"","content":"One thing I find myself with is that Elden Ring has added some significant elements to what I think those who advocate for and provide comfort to the living dead might look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T19:08:34-07:00","id":1513593,"title":"","content":"I was never able to get into the Abyssals because they always felt too deliberately villainous to me. Even Infernals, in my opinion, had more depth and dimension and room for complex motivations, while previous Abyssal books left me with the impression there was nothing more to them than selfishness that makes them willing to commit omnicide as long as they're the last one gobbled up by the Void. So I'd like to see variety and depth added to Abyssals, something that allows me to better understand and sympathize with any given Abyssal than I was able to do in previous editions.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure how I feel about any of the Deathlords. I know being a ghost makes you a one-note instrument, but I just never liked any of them, and felt actively embarrassed by a couple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T20:50:32-07:00","id":1513744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1513593#post1513593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was never able to get into the Abyssals because they always felt too deliberately villainous to me. Even Infernals, in my opinion, had more depth and dimension and room for complex motivations, while previous Abyssal books left me with the impression there was nothing more to them than selfishness that makes them willing to commit omnicide as long as they're the last one gobbled up by the Void. So I'd like to see variety and depth added to Abyssals, something that allows me to better understand and sympathize with any given Abyssal than I was able to do in previous editions.<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure how I feel about any of the Deathlords. I know being a ghost makes you a one-note instrument, but I just never liked any of them, and felt actively embarrassed by a couple.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will say that your feelings are part of the reason I felt that Redemption was an important part of the concept; the idea that you could look back on your mistake and reject nihilism as a death knight to become what is the closest thing to a paladin in setting softens the whole &quot;evil homicidal psychopath&quot; bit. <br /> It may also be why 3rd ed claims they are going for more of a &quot;gothic knightly romance&quot; vibe. King Arthur meets Orpheus is sort of the impression I have going forward and a LOT of that comes from 3rd ed Abyssals being tied more to the Deathlords rather the Neverborn...though yes, the Deathlords need a facelift too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T04:39:55-07:00","id":1521370,"title":"","content":"I really want to actually see Abyssal Medicine done well for a change, I got the impression Neph didn't especially like the concept of the world killing weapons playing doctor and squandered a lot of potential that way. I've done a lot of custom charms for it over the years that essentially lean into the idea of someone who holds your life in your hands that you wish didn't one of my favourite is a reference to Dr Talos from the Book of the New Sun series. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T06:22:15-07:00","id":1521747,"title":"","content":"The biggest thing I want out of Abyssals in 3e is for the old dichotomy to die. It used to be that there were only two concepts that were viable. Either you were a loyalist and so actively working to destroy everything or you were a renegade struggling for redemption. If you tried to do anything else, you had a Deathlord trying to drag you back in line and your very existence was a slow poison that was going to gradually rot Creation away through Resonance. There wasn't room for characters that weren't either for or against the Deathlords. Those that were against the Deathlords also had to be struggling to turn back into Solars, as otherwise they were still going to kill all they cared about.<br /> <br /> There needs to be more than sociopaths and angsty rebels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T01:16:38-07:00","id":1521806,"title":"","content":"Another ability I think was done a little dirty is Bureaucracy. <br /> In 2nd edition especially it's just villain-coded Solar Bureaucracy i.e. Speed the Wheels but you need to kill a henchman like you're a James Bond villain but there's some interesting ways in which I think Bureaucracy could interact with the concept of Grave Goods. In particular I love the imagery of a Deathknight who amasses their wealth in tombs and graves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-04T13:58:22-07:00","id":1522070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1513744#post1513744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say that your feelings are part of the reason I felt that Redemption was an important part of the concept; the idea that you could look back on your mistake and reject nihilism as a death knight to become what is the closest thing to a paladin in setting softens the whole &quot;evil homicidal psychopath&quot; bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is the exact reason for why i strongly disliked the Redemption the way it was presented. Because it implied that being exalted as an Abyssal was a mistake and the only good choice you could make was to somehow &quot;fix&quot; it. Which might seem fine for a purely antagonist group, but is not really a good narrative approach for a choice available for players. because it also implied that the <i>player</i> made a wrong choice, and they should have decided upon a different splat instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><i>The difference between fiction and reality? Fiction has to make sense.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/434-astralporing","name":"Astralporing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-04T17:20:17-07:00","id":1522078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astralporing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1522070#post1522070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that is the exact reason for why i strongly disliked the Redemption the way it was presented. Because it implied that being exalted as an Abyssal was a mistake and the only good choice you could make was to somehow &quot;fix&quot; it. Which might seem fine for a purely antagonist group, but is not really a good narrative approach for a choice available for players. because it also implied that the <i>player</i> made a wrong choice, and they should have decided upon a different splat instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>The good news is that <i>Crucible of Legends</i> makes it clear that is a false dichotomy in 3e by design, not only implication. &quot;Death's Lawgivers&quot; is called out explicitly as <u>renegade</u> option.<br /> So clearly the current team must have felt that concept should have more support.<br /> <br /> I look forward to seeing what 3e comes up with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T23:41:01-08:00","id":1525156,"title":"","content":"Per <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/below-the-quartz-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">this week's Monday Meeting</a>, the crowdfunding art's off to Paradox for approval, and the Indiegogo campaign could be as early as Thursday 16th (myself, I'd play it safe and guess sometime in the 16th-21st range, so it doesn't run into Christmas).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T10:20:04-08:00","id":1525170,"title":"","content":"And of course I just ran into a couple of big expenses<br /> <br /> Ah well, such is life? I'll see what I can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25545-jollycooperative","name":"jollycooperative","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T11:46:20-08:00","id":1525529,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.indiegogo.com/projects/abyssals-sworn-to-the-grave-for-exalted-3e/x/25998874#/\" target=\"_blank\">And the campaign's up and funded.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T14:14:15-08:00","id":1525538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1525529#post1525529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://www.indiegogo.com/projects/abyssals-sworn-to-the-grave-for-exalted-3e/x/25998874#/\" target=\"_blank\">And the campaign's up and funded.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>tch, Sidereal got there first.<br /> <br /> First 2 Stretch Goals hit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T14:16:13-08:00","id":1525540,"title":"","content":"If you back, beware of Indiegogo slipping a huge tip for itself into your bill at the last second. If you have already backed, check your email to see that you haven't inadvertently given IndieGoGo $25 or more of your money. You can cancel your pledge and pledge again without supporting this sort of scam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T16:54:17-08:00","id":1525554,"title":"","content":"Since I've bought myself an Underworld beastie, I've got to try and figure out what I'd want that to actually be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T04:11:51-08:00","id":1525631,"title":"","content":"I listened to the developer interview on the Story Told Podcast and I I think that we have a lot of good stuff to look forward to, especially the redesign of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> But\u2026 I am really underwhelmed by the art that I have seen so far.<br /> <br /> I have always loved how outrageous every single Abyssal looked. Everyone was very clearly a creature of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> The characters in the campaign seem very bland.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T06:10:23-08:00","id":1525633,"title":"","content":"I think it's nice to have a spectrum that includes an end where there are Abyssals with some subtlety to their appearance. I think the premise that they're all incredibly extra limits the range of situations they can be fit into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T11:38:15-08:00","id":1525650,"title":"","content":"Also, there's a fair share of OTT-looking Abyssals in the art, so it's not like they've removed that part of the spectrum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T13:53:03-08:00","id":1525656,"title":"","content":"Anyway, my thoughts on the first half of the first chapter.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Okay, good introduction to the concept. I'm glad that it's not shying away from the fact that becoming Abyssal has eschatonic connotations, but still elaborates on the nuances to how and why one might embrace that. The comment about secrets is particularly compelling, that idea that one might see the offer as an opportunity to gain deeper insight into the nature of the cosmos.<br /> <br /> And lexicon providing a good hint at the new approach to the Underworld. I imagine the ritual afterlives will provide some basis for still having areas that bear a resemblance to one or more places in Creation, while the primeval ones seem like something that can make the ghostly experience very vivid for Abyssals to engage with. Something that sets potential empire building apart from the likes of the Realm in a big way.<br /> <br /> Hmm, intrigued by this line about the Deathlords being <i>entrusted</i> with the Abyssals. The implication that the Neverborn have their hands on the reins a bit more.<br /> <br /> Glad that the iconography of the Monstrance of Celestial Portion is still present, to distinguish these Exalted and provide something tangible for how the Deathlords engage with Choosing them.<br /> <br /> I find myself thinking about how a more nebulous Underworld will help allow the boundaries of shadowlands to finally make sense. I could never really get where the place one would normally cross into in the Underworld would go at night.<br /> <br /> I like what Revolutionary Girl Utena says about the tone and pageantry that will be evoked by Abyssals, a bit more of the surreal romanticism over just being bleak and grim. And yeah, Dark Souls has been creeping into my hopes for this for some time now.<br /> <br /> Ah, okay, so the basic history behind the Abyssal Exalted is still the same. I'll admit, the escape of the Solars still coming from the Deathlords getting hold of the Jade Prison is a bit more conventional than I would have liked, not least because I genuinely do feel it reduces some of the mythic impact of their returning to Creation at an hour of need. Still, I'll at least say that it paints a very vivid picture of the process utilised by the Deathlords to achieve that feat, the grandeur of their combined mystical efforts that would be necessary to acquire it. And I am ultimately glad that the Neverborn are presented as not really being able to function as articulate or calculating masters. The picture of what the Deathlords have done since the Usurpation is also nice, a good balance of being active but cautious in the face of who could oppose them. I do umabiguously still like the feature of the Yozis being involved, the kind of unbreakable deal behind how they'll get their own Exalted.<br /> <br /> I recall some people wanting to expand the parameters of the Bleak Exaltation, but personally I think the premise is vivid enough to stand on its own, that it would be distilled a bit if there was something like a metaphorical death it could go to. It's such a strong set piece, and it gets to be uniquely their own. I like how some of the snapshots get to convey a sense of the perspective the Deathlords might have on their potential Chosen, mortals that impress even them in the manner of their death. The one whose first thought goes to the duty to slay birds is oddly endearing.<br /> <br /> I think there's something worthwhile in the idea that the Abyssals are more at home in the Underworld, but a careful balancing act to make that premise diverse and ultimately playable; I've often thought about that point of how one doesn't want to discourage the wandering lethal swordsman over the person who builds missiles in shadowlands. I think presenting a tone of how the living world doesn't seem comfortable or natural to them would be an effective way to accomplish that, something where it's perfectly possible to play an individual whose adventures are primarily in Creation, and they're kind of grim and moody the whole time. On that note, I have a good feeling about presenting the obligation to the Neverborn by way of the Great Curse; something to feel less like a pressure that builds in them when they don't follow certain rules until it explodes and more like an uncanny weirdness that haunts them for trying to deviate from the dread oath they swore.<br /> <br /> And the thing about adorning themselves in trappings of death... I think that touches on how for all that it can tell serious stories with deep characters and real messages, there's still something a little bit silly about pulp. The idea that they're most comfortable if dressed in funeral garb or hanging out in mausoleums, it's like... it can be over the top in a way that ought to be embraced, trying hard while being unashamed of that. At the same time, I do think it creates a very visceral sense for what the Abyssals need to go through to function, with a nice sprinkle of the native mysticism of the setting to let it be something people can portray in-character with a straight face. On the other hand, I think one can get a lot out of how their Essence Fever isn't &quot;destroy everything&quot; so much as &quot;be urged to your most impressive while your most intense emotions and darkest impulses are at work&quot;. The kind of thing that can let one play an Abyssal who isn't some all-encompassing monster, but has their personality flaws and something that empowers them along those lines.<br /> <br /> I am glad that the presentation of past lives does seem to emphasize some of what I wanted of Abyssals as the presentation of Solars returned from the grave, that sense that the memory of the Usurpation can be vivid enough to inspire the newly Chosen to embody that vengeance or reclamation. An organic way to embody the motif, while also being able to emphasize the character of the actual newly empowered person in question.<br /> <br /> The idea that the Deathlords see the Abyssals as people to instruct in their ways has been talked up for years now. The presentation of the Deathlords being enamoured of their Exalted as the most capable agents for achieving their own dreams is the sort of elaboration of that which I would have inferred from the similar modification to Sidereals. But the idea that they are motivated and struggle to form intimate relationships with them is the most surprising thing and feels like the major game changer. For one thing, it gets to me hard owing to a recent historical kick that has emphasized just how much being a liege required cultivating a personal relationship with vassals, so that awareness and using that to provide depth to the premise is pretty cool. And I'm somebody who's always thought that the Deathlords should be more ghostly than just people in scary costumes, so I think this presentation actually not only makes that stronger, but imposes an interesting and compelling challenge upon them. I think there's so much that can be done to make Deathlords a major and versatile presence in the experience of playing Abyssals that they recognise a need for cultivating a genuine sense of loyalty, and have their own challenges in accomplishing that.<br /> <br /> And indeed, if one has many different Deathknights, one might need to present a few different faces, or at least variations on the same face.<br /> <br /> I find the elaboration given to the debut of the Deathknight to make a very strong case for making their first meeting with their liege something to play out, rather than relegate to the backstory. The journey a unique adventure in its own right, that can culminate in something to let the Deathlord make a very strong first impression. Also seems like a great hook to bring circles together, to have multiple separate journeys that confer before arriving at the lord's citadel. A grand tour of the Underworld following training is all well and good as a device to start introducing ghostly society, but I like it most as something that gives a bit of nuance to the culture and methods of the Deathlords, makes them feel a bit more like thoughtful people, and even implies a bit of attachment to their domains.<br /> <br /> Overall, I think a very strong picture is given here for the manner in which Deathlords build a cohesion for their Exalted, to bind them into larger organisation and cultivate their most useful talents. It lends credibility to how and why Abyssals might be utilised in that manner, and a solid picture for what players might actually do in that position. Indeed, I already see an aspirational hook to being started out with the more minor assignments and wanting to prove oneself capable of the greater responsibilities or more autonomy.<br /> <br /> I hadn't expected the chivalry of death to be something so significant to the Deathlords themselves, but seeing it laid out like this almost makes me think its cooler on them than the Exalted. For a start, I really like the picture of how for all their power and terrible intent, there's something inescapably grim about being a Deathlord if you need to be occupied for ages trying to discern the nature of the commandments bestowed by gods who are dead and dreaming, especially when the punishments for failure are so horrific. I like the potential it lends to how Deathlords are occupied, the enigmas that can come from whether any given manoeuvre accomplishes their own goals, the directives of their masters, or is just about trying to deepen their understanding. I've always been a bit uncertain about the First and Forsaken Lion of limited commitment, but the notion that he still prioritises his own endeavours while being gloomily bound within the restrictions and obligations of his own liege is a great way to bring a lot of life to that. And yeah, I do think it's a great way to provide a foundation for their different characterisation as masters among the dead that remains distinct from something as obvious as patronising different forms of death.<br /> <br /> As for the substance of the chivalry of death, I'm all for something that pushes the ultimate culmination of Abyssal goals off into the furthest future, to give them more room to play around in. As somebody who was distinctly unimpressed by the whole &quot;Chosen of Murder&quot; thing because murdering the majority of people was super easy for the most basic powers they had, I love the notion that the Neverborn seem to have a specific preference for focusing on the most challenging targets that will have the biggest impact over indiscriminate slaughter. Mind, I think that itself can imply some more elaboration over merely killing, even after a challenging fight; to target somebody who is no great trouble physically, but has an impact on the lives of others that makes them worth gradually dismantling in order to create shockwaves through a community. I think that can go far darker for somebody that is into that, while providing for a lot of intricacy and investment over the single dice roll that could end them at once.<br /> <br /> Although sure, breaking down the boundaries between living and dead also provides a huge amount to work with that might be less bleak, and can instead emphasize the gothic beauty of the Underworld and the strange serenity that can come from embracing death, the motifs of accepting its universality.<br /> <br /> I think the end of describing the Abyssals on board with the deathknight role is a good breaking point, I'll get back to the rest of chapter one later.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T19:59:16-08:00","id":1525671,"title":"","content":"I am so impressed with the Deathlords. The changes will take some getting used to, but the bulk of those &quot;changes&quot; is making their histories and true identities foggier and open to storyteller design. In particular, the ill-fated romance between Mask of Winters and Walker in Darkness was almost the extent of the characterization I remembered of either of them beyond Big Bad Evil Guy. But seeing them in context WITHOUT the history really made them unique. In particular, I love Walker as this seductive gothic romance paladin. To me, he really stands out as the beauty and chivalry of death, an impression I didn't get in previous editions.<br /> <br /> The complete rework of Eye and Seven is expected. They are practically a new character, but honestly its for the best. Anyone overly attached to their.. questionable presentation in 2e can probably somehow fit that backstory in. I might reference it if somehow it becomes relevant in any way. But honestly, Eye does a much better job being an actual character this time around. The Deathlords absolutely NEEDED a cackling mad scientist.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the alteration of the Black Heron makes her feel much more useful in play as an actual character rather than a subplot that serves to make two relatively boring Deathlords into a servicable idea. Her entry being the first really hammered home the idea that these Deathlords have been refreshed and remodelled in a good way. And the Deathlords NEEDED a serial killing harlequin.<br /> <br /> All in all, much like the Dynastic Houses, I can actually get some mileage out of literally every Deathlord this time around. Choosing a liege for my Abyssal NPC is actually somewhat of a struggle, and isn't just defaulted to the nearest one. The only Deathlord I wasn't as pleased with was the Silver Prince, because his rather pointless and silly &quot;Im going to pretend to die, then pretend to reincarnate and come back later&quot; subplot was kind of neat, even if I couldnt for the life of me explain any reason for him to do so. Maybe it IS for the best that it was trimmed off. Can't wait for the Underworld writeup!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T03:48:33-08:00","id":1525680,"title":"","content":"The Eye and Seven Despairs rework was really great and created a whole new niche within the Deathlords as both an enemy and an antagonist, plus the Cold House as a location is superb on top of that. The Heron's new situation keeps with her underdog spirit while still giving her more agency to interact with the rest of the Underworld / her Abyssals and makes for an interesting force in Creation/the Underworld. These two are very good glow ups.<br /> <br /> The Lover was fairly underwhelming on the other hand, not particularly evocative as a mentor or a villain beyond just being an obligatory inclusion. The base concept is a little too standard and the execution doesn't do much to elevate it to parity with the other Deathlords. The Tear Eaters were fairly interesting, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T06:46:41-08:00","id":1525685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1525650#post1525650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, there's a fair share of OTT-looking Abyssals in the art, so it's not like they've removed that part of the spectrum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some are better/worse than others, of course, but the ones I am seeing are all solidly in the category of Just a Dude (m/f).<br /> <br /> I have clicked where it says \u201cStory\u201d on the front page and scrolled to the bottom. Am I missing someone? Who stands out to you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":864,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","user":"Jutlander","date":". 11-20-2023, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T10:57:34-08:00","id":1525691,"title":"","content":"The new Underworld is what I was looking forward to the most in 3E Abyssals, and I was not disappointed. This is really good stuff.<br /> Kudos to the writers. The Underworld is finally a place you'd actually want to visit now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","user":"NullApostle","date":". 11-21-2023, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T11:48:36-08:00","id":1525692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jutlander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1525685#post1525685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some are better/worse than others, of course, but the ones I am seeing are all solidly in the category of Just a Dude (m/f).<br /> <br /> I have clicked where it says \u201cStory\u201d on the front page and scrolled to the bottom. Am I missing someone? Who stands out to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm looking at the campaign video.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T12:27:48-08:00","id":1525693,"title":"","content":"Also looking at the campaign video, it looks like Inigo Montoya would be very, very interested to know where the Physician was 20 years ago...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T09:57:58-08:00","id":1525734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1525692#post1525692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm looking at the campaign video.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there's definitely some better art in there.<br /> <br /> TBH the splat iconics across all three editions have, IMO, almost always been unmemorably bland unless they're painfully mockable. Pretty much only Panther, Jade, the Seven-Degreed Physician of Black Maladies (who, even then, invites comparisons to Wario), Mnemon, Peleps Deled, and The Roseblack (and the latter two I <i>forgot were DB signature characters</i> until reminded) have managed to squeeze through the middle for me. Manoqsue Cyan only sticks out in my memory because her archetype is the sort of thing I go for a lot, and Prince Diamond for the trans representation*.<br /> <br /> The new Abyssal iconics definitely seem to lean toward the bland side, but IMO that only sticks out because the prior crew was the most flamboyant of their editions.<br /> <br /> *Though as a trans person I am somewhat conflicted on that due to the Delzhan construction of gender in the first place, but that's definitely off-topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T11:22:33-08:00","id":1525737,"title":"","content":"Honestly, even for the people saying they dislike the signatures, to phrase that in terms of &quot;the art&quot;...<br /> <br /> What exactly is the objection to creepy mask person and blue hood and cloak with wry grin striding past kneeling subjects with dark skies in the background? Riding the meat dragon to attack city walls with a whip of black barbs? The short, large woman with elaborately detailed tunic summoning a monster centipede? The Seven-Degreed Physician at work on his latest cobbled together monstrosity? Elderly warrior on a phone of attack chains? The damn galley, accompanied by a giant ghost snake, sailing towards an island impaled by an enormous sword with a city on the hilt guard?<br /> <br /> Is none of that Exalted enough for people?<br /> <br /> Even if a person dislikes the signatures, how are they not a fucking outlier? How are people noticing them next to all the rest of that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T12:06:09-08:00","id":1525741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1525737#post1525737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, even for the people saying they dislike the signatures, to phrase that in terms of &quot;the art&quot;...<br /> <br /> What exactly is the objection to creepy mask person and blue hood and cloak with wry grin striding past kneeling subjects with dark skies in the background? Riding the <b>meat dragon</b> to attack city walls with a whip of black barbs?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;CAAAARL! They surrendered already!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oops, my bad! I heard 'surrender' and parsed it as 'sir, render them!'&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;And what's with the whips? Those are incredibly impractical in a fight!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Fight? Who said anything about a fight? This is a massacre!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You planned this, didn't you Carl? You were never going to accept a surrender.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's not my fault! It's the Whispers!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You've never done anything according to the Whispers!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, maybe they should speak up.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-21T12:23:07-08:00","id":1525743,"title":"","content":"This guy gets it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T14:17:41-08:00","id":1525885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1525554#post1525554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I've bought myself an Underworld beastie, I've got to try and figure out what I'd want that to actually be.</div> </div> </div> </div>...maybe something that would be a sneaky way to get some new lore, like an Alaun ghost or something like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T04:31:16-08:00","id":1525906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1525885#post1525885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...maybe something that would be a sneaky way to get some new lore, like an Alaun ghost or something like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a priority for me at all.<br /> <br /> My mind keeps going back to that skeleton snake from the Shadowman video game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T07:43:31-08:00","id":1525908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1525737#post1525737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, even for the people saying they dislike the signatures, to phrase that in terms of &quot;the art&quot;...<br /> <br /> What exactly is the objection to creepy mask person and blue hood and cloak with wry grin striding past kneeling subjects with dark skies in the background? Riding the meat dragon to attack city walls with a whip of black barbs? The short, large woman with elaborately detailed tunic summoning a monster centipede? The Seven-Degreed Physician at work on his latest cobbled together monstrosity? Elderly warrior on a phone of attack chains? The damn galley, accompanied by a giant ghost snake, sailing towards an island impaled by an enormous sword with a city on the hilt guard?<br /> <br /> Is none of that Exalted enough for people?<br /> <br /> Even if a person dislikes the signatures, how are they not a fucking outlier? How are people noticing them next to all the rest of that?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;But my EDGYYYYYYYY!&quot; Okay, I'm being reductive, but a lot of them seem to think the Falling Tears Poet should be the baseline...not realizing that means Lady of Midnight in Bloodstained Robes is also an assumed default (hint - she's the one using chains for a bikini).<br /> <br /> Also, the recent spoiler showed that trappings of death can be very subtle - with that in mind, I actually really like the iconics, because the more casual ones seem like the social ones...the ones who want to come off as disarming and friendly, in other words, or be otherwise unbothered. It's not artists being lazy, it's characters being sneaky.<br /> <br /> The skull mask is for when it's time for the gloves to come off or you're already in a place where people see the Romantic ghost overlord and instinctively bow before the Shining One.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 11-25-2023, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T12:12:32-08:00","id":1525916,"title":"","content":"Speaking of, one of those signatures looks like a blue colour version of Dr Henry Killinger, so I don't know what people object to there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T09:21:25-08:00","id":1526071,"title":"","content":"Here's hoping Occult or Presence have something to buff up ghosts, so that we can turn our ghost-Gollums into proper Nazg\u00fbl.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T12:05:11-08:00","id":1526243,"title":"","content":"Presence has sexy vampire Charms, so that's nice. I like that the old &quot;more pretty or horrifying with rising Essence&quot; still exists in the form of Death's Unholy Visage.<br /> <br /> Night-Horror Summons is weird; I like it.<br /> <br /> Melee is worth it simply for Soul-Drinking Blade.<br /> <br /> Occult, however, is a big disappointment. I like the Whispers-boosting effects of Howling Silence Meditation, and the telepathy Charms, but otherwise it is largely a retread of Solar Occult. The necromancy Charms likewise just feel like buffed versions of the Lunar sorcery Charms, rather than adding any unique capabilities for the Abyssal necromancer; hopefully, War has something to net you more zombies when you raise them by any means.<br /> I'm also mildly confused that there's a mirror to Soul Projection Method, but nothing comparable to Ephemeral Induction Technique. Don't get me wrong, I <i>like</i> Soul Projection/Domination Method, but I like EIT more, and I don't think the Cantata of Empty Voice-alike of Life-Annihilating Susurrus can compare.<br /> Actually, you know what would be cool? Something to build on Spirit-Devouring Appetite to make like the Bishop and turn into a whole freakish ghost-beast from the spirits you've devoured.<br /> <br /> The fleshcrafting in Medicine, other than Necrotic Graft Technique, is really underwhelming. 5m for a E3 Charm to make a zombie, when a Midnight and anyone with Barrow-King's Authority can do it instantly for 1m? <i>Essence 5</i> to make a zombie cool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T12:30:54-08:00","id":1526244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1526243#post1526243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fleshcrafting in Medicine, other than Necrotic Graft Technique, is really underwhelming. 5m for a E3 Charm to make a zombie, when a Midnight and anyone with Barrow-King's Authority can do it instantly for 1m? <i>Essence 5</i> to make a zombie cool?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're still missing pieces of the puzzle there - that tree works on zombies or other reanimated corpses, and we still don't know what Necromancy has for weird high-investment corpse-horrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-07T18:19:54-08:00","id":1526485,"title":"","content":"I did like the usability upgrade they put into Nightmare-Carving Murmur; I'm definitely going to apply that as a Homebrew for Wyld-Shaping Technique (although I'd prefer to see an official errata for that <i>a la</i> the Artifact rules in <b>Arms of the Chosen</b>, but I'll take what I can get).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T05:40:20-08:00","id":1526921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1526243#post1526243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fleshcrafting in Medicine, other than Necrotic Graft Technique, is really underwhelming. 5m for a E3 Charm to make a zombie, when a Midnight and anyone with Barrow-King's Authority can do it instantly for 1m? <i>Essence 5</i> to make a zombie cool?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there's a whole other way it could've gone after Necrotic Graft Technique that I'd have enjoyed much more.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the Abyssal Doctor invoking the cultural association between healers and witches with some nods to the shady side of modern medical practices. Your child is sick and unlikely to survive, so you turn to a person that under ordinary circumstances you'd stay the hell away from. This will cost you <i>greatly</i> but really, what choice do you have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T20:34:43-08:00","id":1526962,"title":"","content":"If you have an issue with a charm compared to other charms, maybe put it in the review form? It is one of the reasons they do that in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-18T07:18:11-08:00","id":1527050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1526921#post1526921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, there's a whole other way it could've gone after Necrotic Graft Technique that I'd have enjoyed much more.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the Abyssal Doctor invoking the cultural association between healers and witches with some nods to the shady side of modern medical practices. Your child is sick and unlikely to survive, so you turn to a person that under ordinary circumstances you'd stay the hell away from. This will cost you <i>greatly</i> but really, what choice do you have?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Much can be done about your height. Are you familiar with the... abominable sciences?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-27T12:39:42-08:00","id":1527511,"title":"","content":"It's long been a subject of morbid fascination as to what exactly Dr Talos did to Jolenta to make her beautiful and the consequences (Gene Wolfe's Book of the New Sun series, for the unfamiliar).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-28T11:01:35-08:00","id":1527561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1527050#post1527050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Much can be done about your height. Are you familiar with the... abominable sciences?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly on topic, but this makes me think of my mother's experience with doctors suggesting to remove part of her femurs because she was 'too tall' (6'1&quot;).<br /> <br /> Well, I suppose it is, because standards are always relative, and people in the real world have gone to some horrifying extremes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T19:06:02-07:00","id":1545186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1527561#post1527561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly on topic, but this makes me think of my mother's experience with doctors suggesting to remove part of her femurs because she was 'too tall' (6'1&quot;).<br /> <br /> Well, I suppose it is, because standards are always relative, and people in the real world have gone to some horrifying extremes...</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of an actual doctor suggesting such a thing out of the blue is disconcerting on all kind of levels, like health <i>and policing someone else's appearance</i> go hand in hand, what is unconfortable in far too many levels. Also touches on the mindset that inspired a lot of eugenics nonsense from the 19th and early 20th centuries, though medieval/renaissance societies had their own brand of physiognomic nonsense with the four humours theory, that possibly might be adaptable into Creation as some sort of idea inspired by elementalism &amp; geomancy, i guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway and back on the subject of Abyssals, what do we have on the Deathknights and supposed origins in 3e, any major divergences from previous editions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T00:46:52-07:00","id":1545200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1545186#post1545186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway and back on the subject of Abyssals, what do we have on the Deathknights and supposed origins in 3e, any major divergences from previous editions?</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of origins, the only notable difference is that because the location of the Jade Prison was different (hidden in the constellation of the Mask), the method of getting it was different, involving the Calendar of Setesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T02:51:46-07:00","id":1545204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1500606-abyssals-are-coming?p=1545200#post1545200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In terms of origins, the only notable difference is that because the location of the Jade Prison was different (hidden in the constellation of the Mask), the method of getting it was different, involving the Calendar of Setesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>But still a thing of &quot;just about a few years before the present, or the Scarlet Empress' disappearance at most&quot;, in terms of timeline then? So no rogue elder abyssals without a lot of lore gymnastics or some such still.<br /> <br /> Well, no big deal either way, with Liminals, Lunars accessing 2nd circle necromancy in 3e and the occasional goth/creeper exigent, there can be plenty to occupy, harass and distract the Deathlords with before the new kids' coming....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 11-02-2024, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T12:48:36-07:00","id":1545218,"title":"","content":"Here's something you might be interested in: Shortly after discovering the Well of Udr, the Dowager tried testing its power by infiltrating Stygia to hunt the Dual Monarchs. In response, they used the Calendar of Setesh as a weapon against her, and it took seven years for the Neverborn to resurrect her. On top of that, she came back with most of her original personality flensed away, now a true servant of the Neverborn, pursuing the destruction of Creation - oracular, lost in frequent reveries, sometimes convinced that Creation is a construct of her nightmarish whim, sometimes a pitiless, hateful, hungry hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}